+# Marginalia Books
+
+A static website for Marginalia Books, a fictional independent bookshop. It has four pages (home, books, events and visit) with a shared navigation, a genre-filterable catalog, an events list, opening hours and a contact form.
+
+The site is plain HTML, CSS and vanilla JavaScript with no build step and no external requests. Everything in it is fictional: the address (14 Example Row), the 555 phone number and the `.test` email domain.
+
+## Run it locally
+
+From the repository root:
+
+```sh
+python3 -m http.server 8000
+```
+
+Then open <http://localhost:8000/>.
+
+## Run the tests
+
+The tests use headless Chromium through the preinstalled `playwright` module and start their own static server on a free port. No packages need installing.
+
+```sh
+node tests/run.mjs                 # all tests
+node tests/run.mjs books           # only test files whose name contains "books"
+```
+
+## Layout
+
+- `index.html`, `books.html`, `events.html`, `visit.html`: the four pages.
+- `css/styles.css`: the single shared stylesheet.
+- `js/nav.js`: menu button for narrow screens.
+- `js/books.js`: genre filter, state kept in the `genre` query parameter.
+- `js/visit.js`: today's hours and contact form validation (the form sends nothing).
+- `tests/`: Playwright tests, one file per area.
